-- title:
--   Integrality shape for the weight-m floor Riemann–Roch space
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and let $F$ be an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ over $K$. Let $y \in F$ be an element whose image in $K((q))$ is the series [`ModularCurve.jqModC K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), namely $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $K$ of the power series $E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-24}$-type numerator `jNum`; assume $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K(y)$ generated by $y$. Let $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $D$ be a divisor on $F/K$, i.e. a finitely supported integer-valued function on the places $w$ of $F/K$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $K$, distinct from $F$, and principal ideal rings), such that for every $w$, $D(w)$ is the sum of $(2m\,\mathrm{ord}_w y)/3$ when $\mathrm{ord}_w y > 0$ and $0$ otherwise, $(m\,\mathrm{ord}_w(y-1728))/2$ when $\mathrm{ord}_w(y-1728) > 0$ and $0$ otherwise, and $m\,\mathrm{ord}_w y$ when $\mathrm{ord}_w y < 0$ and $0$ otherwise; here $\mathrm{ord}_w$ is minus the logarithm of the adic valuation at $w$, and the quotients are integer division, hence floors for these non-negative numerators. Let $G \in F$ lie in the Riemann–Roch space of $D$, i.e. $w(G) \le \exp(D(w))$ for every place $w$. Then, writing $j$ for [`ModularCurve.jqModC K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) and viewing $G$ in $K((q))$: $G^6 j^{4m}(j-1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $G^2 j^{m}(j-1728)^{m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the level-free form of the statement that an element of the weight-$m$ floor Riemann–Roch space has the integrality (holomorphy) shape of a weight-$2m$ modular function on the two standard charts of the $j$-line, the two conjuncts being integrality over $K[j]$ and over $K[j^{-1}]$. It is used in the proofs of the lower bounds for the dimensions of spaces of modular forms of even and of odd weight on $\Gamma_1$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isIntegral_and_isIntegral_of_mem_riemannRochSpace_weightFloor.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_JqCoeff
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
